{"name":"False Cypress","hex":"#939b88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"false cypress","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any conifer of the genus Chamaecyparis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/false_cypress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chamaecyparis","blocks":[{"text":"Chamaecyparis, the false-cypresses, is a genus of conifers in the cypress family Cupressaceae, native to eastern Asia and to the western and eastern margins of the United States. The name is derived from the Greek khamai (χαμαί), meaning \"on the earth\", and kuparissos (κυπάρισσος) for \"cypress\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Sawara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamaecyparis","wikidata":"Q147791"},{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress","wikidata":"Q14169641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/330px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/960px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/330px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AActinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/